{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim's anger was kindled.</b> Because he went with the intention to curse. <b>And the angel of YHWH stood in the way to be an adversary to him.</b> Balaam plied a craft that was not his own — the mouth was given to Jacob, as it says (Genesis 27:22): ״הקול קול יעקב״ — and therefore the angel plied a craft that was not his own, for he was an angel of mercy and became an adversary; as it is written, ״הנה אנכי יצאתי לשטן״ — measure for measure."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:03.873129702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}